'''Mech Patrol Axel''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be obtained by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Justice Strikes Back! Dark Heroes (Gacha Event)|Justice Strikes Back! Dark Heroes]] gacha event. They were added in [[Version 14.0 Update|Version 14.0]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 774
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Mech Patrol Axel
|name2 = Steel Sergeant Axel
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Steel Sergeant Axel''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like all Dark Heroes, Axel's role changes depending on their form. Their DPS is not bad for a unit with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]]-level range. Something to note about both forms is their Conjured Spirit, which lacks other meaningful status effects, but has 40% Metal Killer that can easily decimate tougher [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metals]] such as [[Super Metal Hippoe]], [[Sir Metal Seal]] and [[Metal Cyclone]].

===Normal Form===
Mech Patrol Axel has a very interesting use, which is to inflict various status effects on [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] and Metal enemies from long range. The former can easily be put to good use, as plenty of Aliens are backliners, but Mech Patrol Axel faces rough competition from [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]], who does massive damage instead of status effects. However, Mech Patrol Axel does outclass Aphrodite in generalist damage. Against Metal enemies, Mech Patrol Axel does extremely well as there is little competing for the long-ranged anti-Metal crowd-control niche. They may not be able to [[Critical Hit|Crit]], but when paired with a [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitter]], their crowd-control capabilities become invaluable. Overall, this form is a fairly good long-ranged [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] and an extremely potent anti-Metal crowd controller. Just remember to bring a Critter.

===Evolved Form===
Steel Sergeant Axel trades their Normal Form's abilities for 10% Metal Killer, freeze, and warp immunity. Warp immunity provides a better matchup against [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]], but not much else. Freeze and Metal Killer, on the other hand, are very interesting. Both benefit from multi-hit, as the freeze effectively lasts for 3.67 seconds and the Metal Killer can take 27.1% (plus another 3 HP) of a Metal enemy's current HP. This is a very unique niche, as there are few other long-ranged Alien/Metal freezers and Metal Killer is a rare ability. Use Steel Sergeant Axel if you need backliner damage or if you need to deal some serious damaging or crowd-controlling capabilities against Metal or Alien enemies.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Sniper|EvolvedClass = Backliner & Crowd-Controller & Sniper|TrueClass=|UltraClass=}}
<!--NOTE: Metal Killer takes out 10% of current health, therefore with 3 hits:
100% -> 90% -> 81% -> 72.9%
Thus the total combined hits take out 27.1% of a single Metal's max HP.-->

